# Local development needs almost none of this — a seesaw checkout beside this
# one is enough. The rest is for deployment; the full runbook is in the seesaw
# repo, DOCS.md → Deployment.

# ── Job store ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Postgres, shared with the Python workers. Unset, the store is the seesaw
# checkout's local SQLite file, which is all local development needs.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://...

# ── Artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A seesaw checkout's outputs/, for reading plans and plots locally.
# Defaults to ../seesaw/outputs, so side-by-side checkouts can skip it.
# SEESAW_OUTPUTS_DIR=/absolute/path/to/seesaw/outputs

# ── Running jobs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local mode: point at a seesaw checkout and the dashboard spawns a worker
# itself whenever you create or approve a job. No second terminal.
# SEESAW_REPO_DIR=/absolute/path/to/seesaw

# Interpreter for that worker. Defaults to <SEESAW_REPO_DIR>/.venv/bin/python.
# SEESAW_PYTHON=/absolute/path/to/seesaw/.venv/bin/python

# Modal mode (deployment): the runner's endpoints, from `modal deploy
# orchestrator/modal_app.py`. MODAL_INVOKE_TOKEN must equal its RUNNER_KEY.
# MODAL_RUN_STAGE_URL=https://<account>--seesaw-runner-start.modal.run
# MODAL_ARTIFACT_URL=https://<account>--seesaw-runner-artifact.modal.run
# MODAL_INVOKE_TOKEN=...

# ── Write gate ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set in deployment so the public dashboard is read-only: creating, approving,
# cancelling, and deleting spend real credit. Unset, everything is allowed.
# WRITE_KEY=...
